8. Key Insights
Overall churn rate is 25.2% in the project dataset.
Month-to-month customers have the highest churn rate (33.8%).
Electronic check has the highest churn rate among payment methods (29.0%).
Fiber optic has the highest churn rate among internet-service groups (29.0%).
Lower-tenure customers show higher vulnerability in the generated data.
Security and technical-support services are associated with lower churn in the generated data.
9. Business Recommendations
Create an early-tenure customer engagement program.
Offer suitable incentives for customers considering longer contracts.
Encourage automated payment methods where appropriate.
Promote support and security services to at-risk customers.
Use model-generated risk scores as a prioritization aid rather than as an automatic decision.
10. Limitations and Ethical Considerations
The dataset is synthetic and intended for educational demonstration. Numerical findings must not be interpreted as actual telecom-industry statistics. The model should be validated on genuine organizational data before any real-world use.
11. Conclusion
The project demonstrates an end-to-end Data Analytics and AI workflow: data preparation, EDA, visualization, predictive modeling and interpretation. Machine learning can support retention planning by identifying patterns and prioritizing potentially high-risk accounts.
